# What must never enter the build context.
#
# This file is a security control before it is an optimisation. Everything
# listed here would otherwise be sent to the daemon and be available to any
# COPY - including one added later by someone who did not read the Dockerfile.

# The real secrets. .env holds the Google client secret, the session signing
# key and the database password. It is git-ignored, which says nothing about
# Docker: without this line a `COPY . .` bakes all three into a layer that
# survives deletion in a later step, because layers are not editable.
.env

# A 112 MB virtualenv built for the host's interpreter and the host's
# architecture. The image builds its own; copying this one in would be both
# slow and wrong.
.venv

# Byte code compiled by a different interpreter version.
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache

# Not part of the service.
demo_walkthrough.py
seed_demo.py

# The compose file describes how to run the image; it is not part of it.
docker-compose.yml
